    "stdout": "{\n  \"newProducts\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenGravity\",\n      \"description\": \"A zero-install, BYOK vanilla JS clone of Antigravity - full AI IDE with WebContainer API integration for real terminal environments. Built to avoid usage limits on closed-source AI IDEs.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/ab-613/opengravity\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-11\",\n      \"source\": \"GitHub\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Graphbit PRFlow - AI Code Review Agent\",\n      \"description\": \"AI code review agent that automates PR reviews with workflow orchestration. Integrates into development workflows to catch security issues and learn team standards.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://producthunt.com/posts/graphbit-prflow\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-07\",\n      \"source\": \"Product Hunt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Mi\",\n      \"description\": \"30-line zero-config CLI agent for bug fixes and refactoring. An autonomous coding agent that fits in a single JavaScript file with no framework or dependencies beyond Node builtins. Works with any OpenAI-compatible API (OpenAI, Ollama, local models). Includes bash tool for full system access and skills tool for markdown playbooks loaded on demand. Optimized for running with local LLMs with minimal token usage.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/av/mi\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n      \"source\": \"Product Hunt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Linchpin\",\n      \"description\": \"Open-source, self-hostable runtime for managed AI agents under Apache-2.0 license. Deploy with single 'docker compose up' command to get a full agent platform with REST + SSE API, per-session Docker sandbox, MCP tools, encrypted vaults. Bring any cloud model via OpenRouter or local via Ollama. Includes versioned agent configs, environment templates, 8 built-in tools (bash, read, write, edit, glob, grep, web_fetch, web_search), Fernet-encrypted credential vaults, and event log persistence.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/linchpinhq/linchpin\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n      \"source\": \"Product Hunt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"BossHogg\",\n      \"description\": \"Agent-first CLI for PostHog analytics and feature flags. Gives AI coding agents and terminal-native developers a compact, scriptable way to operate PostHog without loading a large MCP tool surface into every session. Supports HogQL queries, feature flags, persons, groups, cohorts, events, insights, dashboards, experiments, and production-safe analytics operations with --json output, stable error codes, auth redaction, and HTTPS-only releases.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/aaronkwhite/bosshogg-cli\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n      \"source\": \"Product Hunt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"xyOps\",\n      \"description\": \"Open-source operations automation platform for self-hosted teams under BSD-3-Clause license. Schedule jobs, build visual workflows, monitor servers, trigger alerts, capture snapshots, and coordinate incident response from one app. Run plugins written in any language via JSON over STDIO, collect server metrics with xySat, store secrets, buckets, roles, API keys, and web hooks. Full app feature set is open source including SSO - no enterprise fork, no license key, no telemetry. Paid plans are support subscriptions only.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://xyops.io\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-09\",\n      \"source\": \"Product Hunt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Mycelis\",\n      \"description\": \"Serverless AI workspace with smart routing and MCP agents. Abstracts hardware completely - instantly spin up open-source models on optimized GPUs or bring your own keys (BYOK). Acts as unified OpenAI-compatible API gateway for coding clients like OpenCode, desktop apps, or scripts. Features conditional smart routing to optimal models, vector-powered semantic cache to slash costs, integrated RAG, native MCP agents for GitHub/Slack/Discord, and per-minute usage billing with zero server maintenance.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://mycelis.ai\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n      \"source\": \"Product Hunt\"",
